{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והעל", :translit "veha'al", :gloss "and bring up"} {:he "והעל אותם הר ההר", :translit "veha'al otam har hahar", :gloss "and bring them up Mount Hor"} {:he "ואידך", :translit "ve'idach", :gloss "and the other"} {:he "וימותו הצפרדעים מן הבתים מן החצרות ומן השדות", :translit "vayamutu hatzefard'im min habatim min hachatzarot umin hasadot", :gloss "and the frogs died from the houses from the courtyards and from the fields"} {:he "יען לא האמנתם בי להקדישני", :translit "ya'an lo he'emantem bi lehakdisheni", :gloss "because you did not believe in Me to sanctify Me"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והעל" "והעל אותם הר ההר"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud in Pesaḥim 53b asks what reasoning led Ḥananiah, Mishael, and Azariah to surrender themselves to Nebuchadnezzar's fiery furnace (Daniel 3). It answers that they drew a qal va-ḥomer from the frogs of the plague: if frogs, which are not commanded regarding kiddush ha-Shem, voluntarily entered the ovens during the plague, then they who are commanded should do so all the more. The frogs that entered the ovens are inferred from the phrasing of Exodus 8:9 (וימותו הצפרדעים מן הבתים מן החצרות ומן השדות), which omits the ovens from the places the frogs died, implying they survived there. Moses and Aaron, by contrast, did not draw this inference at Mei Merivah; their failure to sanctify God is stated in Numbers 20:12 (ya'an lo he'emantem bi lehakdisheni), and their consequent decree — that they would not enter the Land — follows there.", :sources ["Pesaḥim 53b" "Daniel 3" "Exodus 8:9" "Numbers 20:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והעל" "והעל אותם הר ההר"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "והעל", :refs ["Exodus 8:1" "Numbers 20:25"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והעל אותם הר ההר", :refs ["Numbers 20:25"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:26.352027484Z", :model "glm-5.2"}